King's Table (Commander Duels v0.8.7): allies who take their own turns, a game's own attack rules,
combat across range, and each player's own starting life.

Reason: King's Table is the Emperor variant (rule 809) with house rules: two teams of three, each
player with their own turns and a limited range of influence (801). Patch 0001 names teammates
only for shared team turns (805). This patch adds allies, players of a team who keep their own
turns (Game.getAllies, the teammates by default, so Two-Headed Giant is unchanged): allies are not
opponents, and the computer player neither aims harmful spells at them nor scores their
permanents as an enemy's, and plans its attacks at the players the game lets it attack. It adds a game's own attack rules (Game.attackablePlayers,
Game.attacksOnlyNamedPlayers; 809.4b and the King's house rule); players who face each other in a
combat across range (Game.inCombatAcrossRange), who are opponents for that combat's blocks and
triggers though not for targets and effects; and each player's own starting life total
(Game.getStartingLife(UUID), 103.4), with the cards and the condition that read "your starting life
total" asking for the right player's. Every default keeps XMage's behaviour in other games.
Upstream: none.
Remove when: XMage supports the Emperor variant with these rules itself.

